    "assumptions": [
        "The design target is the 60 W chassis. All three chassis variants are checked because the vendor STEP superimposes them; the upright and side mounts touch only the +Y back wall and the -Z end cap, which every variant shares, so all three must pass.",
        "Envelope and hole values come from params.json via model.py, not from a drawing. Regenerate them if params.json changes: the numbers here are the acceptance contract for the CURRENT parameter set, and a parameter change that moves a hole is supposed to fail this gate until it is reviewed.",
        "cylinder_at points sit on the feature's axis, not on its face: a Y-axis hole is checked by the axis line passing within pos_tol of the given point, which is what catches a correct hole on the wrong side.",
        "The countersinks are cones, not cylinders, so they are not covered by the cylinder checks. Their arithmetic is asserted in code instead \u00e2\u20ac\u201d interface.check_backwall_screw() and check_bottom_screw() raise during the build.",
        "The material_volume band is a 15% sanity range around the built volume, not a drawing requirement, hence soft.",
        "K-factor 0.42 is assumed, not measured. It affects only the developed flat patterns, never the folded solid or any fit result; flat_patterns.py prints it and the bend table carries it so a shop can re-develop with their own.",
        "The hybrid chassis - Tile core plus ONE 60 W fin bank - is not a body in the vendor STEP. It is built from the file's own geometry at the measured split plane |X| = 14.5, and split_variants.fin_bank() raises if that bank ever stops measuring 131921.4 mm3, so a changed vendor file cannot quietly redefine the configuration this plate mounts."
    ],
